\title{Homeomorphism}
\taxon{Definition}
\p{
    A \strong{homeomorphism} between topological spaces #{X} and #{Y} is a
    bijective [continuous map](def-005N) #{f:X\to Y} whose inverse
    #{f^{-1}:Y\to X} is also continuous. If such a map exists, #{X} and #{Y}
    are \strong{homeomorphic}, written #{X\cong Y}.
}
\p{
    A continuous bijection need not be a homeomorphism: continuity controls
    preimages of open sets, whereas continuity of the inverse also requires
    the original map to preserve the topology in the opposite direction.
}
